{
  "tema": 9188,
  "slug": "tampoco",
  "titulo": "Using tampoco for either / neither",
  "subtitulo": "Yo tampoco: the negative partner of también.",
  "foto": "t10.jpg",
  "regla": "Tampoco = either / neither. Before the verb it goes alone (tampoco viene); after the verb, it needs no before the verb (no viene tampoco).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "To say _either_ or _neither_ in a negative sentence, use **tampoco**. It's the negative partner of **también** (_too, also_)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "There are two patterns:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "subject",
            "**tampoco**",
            "affirmative verb"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "subject",
            "**no**",
            "verb",
            "**tampoco**"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "When **tampoco** goes **before** the verb, don't add **no**. When it goes **after** the verb, **no** goes before the verb (a double negative, which is correct in Spanish)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "In the second pattern, **tampoco** can go anywhere after the verb; the meaning doesn't change: **no viene tampoco a la junta**, **no viene a la junta tampoco**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "On its own, as a short answer: **yo tampoco**, **a mí tampoco** (see [[7681|yo también / yo tampoco]])."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **tampoco** is a **no** in disguise. If it walks in first, no other **no** is allowed in the room."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "Beto no viene a la junta y Carolina ==tampoco== viene.",
              "en": "Beto isn't coming to the meeting, and neither is Carolina."
            },
            {
              "es": "Beto no viene a la junta y Carolina no viene ==tampoco==.",
              "en": "Beto isn't coming to the meeting, and Carolina isn't either."
            },
            {
              "es": "Carolina no viene ==tampoco== a la junta.",
              "en": "Carolina isn't coming to the meeting either."
            },
            {
              "es": "—No me gusta el viento. —A mí ==tampoco==.",
              "en": "\"I don't like the wind.\" \"Me neither.\""
            },
            {
              "es": "Holden ==tampoco== sabía nada.",
              "en": "Holden didn't know anything either."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Carolina tampoco no viene."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Carolina tampoco viene."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Carolina no viene tampoco."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Before the verb, **tampoco** goes alone."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "—No tengo hambre. —Yo también."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "—No tengo hambre. —Yo tampoco."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "After a negative, agree with **tampoco**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
